{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T01:32:43Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T01:34:27Z","body":"@clayjohn after going a step farther, I built myself dlink builds as well, to see if i can get a c++ GDExtension in there\n\nNow I have, weirdly, this set:\n\nweb_nothreads: works\nweb_nothreads_dlink: works\nweb: works\nweb_dlink: **does not work**\n\ncan you reproduce this? does this need a new issue? We're on the opposite once again, now that's a *threading* build not working.\n\nI might also be making some mistake building it, which is why I'd rather have a second opinion first. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141852178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141868432","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109148#issuecomment-3141868432","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109148","id":3141868432,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67RRuQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T01:41:32Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T01:41:32Z","body":"I'm not the right person to ask. I just had to look up what dlink builds are haha. \n\nI doubt this is the same issue though. Unless you are using multithreaded rendering or physics. \n\nThere have been a few regressions and regression fixes relating to threaded web builds recently. Mostly dealing with how threads are allocated. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141868432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141898357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109148#issuecomment-3141898357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109148","id":3141898357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67RZB1","user":{"login":"sinni800","id":2879097,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzkwOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2879097?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800","html_url":"https://github.com/sinni800","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinni800/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T01:53:13Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T01:58:11Z","body":"Well, dlink builds... they shouldn't be that different, actually. They just have support for dynamic linking libraries (GDExtensions) on web. \n\nI just have one question, in the code you made, is there any ifdefs or sorts that filter by threading? Is that maybe not triggered when it's a dlink build? That would be the only way it could still be relevant here. \n\nOtherwise, it's a new issue I assume.\n\nTo check for DLINK within c++, it's the define WEB_DLINK_ENABLED. Searching the source though, I only find two occurances\n\nApparently, dlink being enabled also causes \"proxy_to_pthread\" being disabled, which is where we go to threading country again, hm..\n\nAnd this, in turn, causes, according to the emscripten manual:\n\n```\n    -sPROXY_TO_PTHREAD: In this mode your original main() is replaced by a new one that creates a pthread and runs the original main() on it. As a result, your application’s main() is run off the browser main (UI) thread, which is good for responsiveness. The browser main thread does still run code when things are proxied to it, for example to handle events, rendering, etc. The main thread also does things like create pthreads for you, so that you can depend on them synchronously.\n```\n\nSource: https://emscripten.org/docs/porting/pthreads.html\n\nDoes this ring any bells for the worker threads we're discussing here? If the proxy is disabled, the main thread is actually the browser thread. If the proxy is enabled, the main thread is already a separate thread in the browser. I'm poking in the dark, to be honest.\n\nEDIT: proxy_to_pthread is not even enabled by default, so this is the wrong direction i think","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141898357/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3146711581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109148#issuecomment-3146711581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109148","id":3146711581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67jwId","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-02T20:33:36Z","updated_at":"2025-08-02T20:33:36Z","body":"That sounds more likely to be related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104458 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108969 which were recent changes to our threaded web builds","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3146711581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]